The NHS states that adults aged 19 to 64 need about 1.5 micrograms a day of Vitamin B12 (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-b). The NHS also states that taking 2 mg or less a day of Vitamin B12 in supplements is unlikely to cause any harm, and that there is not enough evidence to show what the effects may be of taking high doses of Vitamin B12 supplements (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-b).

